Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 14:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(doctor): read update admission policy through a bounded
 independent reader (#163369)

Doctor update-admission checks hashed the complete shared SQLite artifact family on every assertion (readCurrentOpenClawStateDatabaseContentVersion inside the admission reader), and lease writes invalidated the row cache, so repeated maintenance checks re-hashed archives inside small write transactions and prolonged the Gateway-offline window. The admission reader now holds an independent read-only connection within the schema-maintenance scope and admitted native-source lifetime, reads committed policy in one bounded snapshot per assertion, keeps lease/update admission, quarantine, schema and source-identity checks fresh, and closes before releasing source retention.

Closes #163365

Co-authored-by: victor-gurbani <89997914+victor-gurbani@users.noreply.github.com>
